8087  FSCALE   (x87 coprocessor, 1980)
ST(0)  :=  ST(0)  *  2 ^ trunc(ST(1))
fast scale by power of two  =  add integer N to exponent

TYPES  (internal temporary real, 80 bits)
  bit 79      S     sign
  bits 78-64  E     15-bit exponent, bias 16383
  bits 63-0   F     64-bit significand, explicit integer bit
                    form  1.bbbb...   *  2^(E-16383)
  true exp range    -16382 .. +16383
  extra datapath    G R S  (guard, round, sticky) for rounding

TAGS  (2 bits per stack slot)
  00  valid
  01  zero
  10  special   (NaN / Inf / denorm / unsupported)
  11  empty

STACK / VARIABLES
  ST(0)  value to scale          -> tmpA
  ST(1)  scale factor N          -> tmpB
  tmpA, tmpB     80-bit temps + tag
  tmpC           64-bit frac temp / constant hold
  Breg / sumreg  adder operands
  expConv        exponent converter  (specials, ovf, unf)
  stackPtr       TOS pointer, 8-deep stack
  shifter        64-bit left/right barrel
  adder          ~69-bit, cin=1 used for subtract

CORE MATH
  value  =  S * F * 2^(E - 16383)
  FSCALE adds integer N to E, leaves F and S alone
  N comes from ST(1) by converting its significand to int:
      shift_count  =  0x403E - ST(1).exp
      0x403E       =  63 + 16383   =  16446
      shift right F by (63 - true_exp) bits
  if ST(1) negative:  E := E - N   (adder cin=1)
  else:               E := E + N

MICROCODE SKETCH  (entry #0748)
  ST(0) -> tmpA
  if tmpA tag ZERO     bail
  ST(1) -> tmpB
  if tmpB tag ZERO     bail
  if empty/special     call SPECIAL_TMPS
  load const 0x403E
  convert tmpB frac -> integer N via shifter
  add/sub N to tmpA.exp
  expConv checks overflow / underflow
  if abnormal          call NONNORMAL_RESULT / CREATE_DENORM
  tmpA -> ST(0)
  RNI

SPECIAL CASES
  zero * anything     -> 0
  empty register      -> invalid exception
  NaN / Inf / denorm  -> SPECIAL_TMPS
  overflow            -> Inf or max (mask dependent)
  underflow           -> denorm or 0
  negative N          -> subtract from exponent

COMPLEXITY
  140+ micro-instructions
  3 subroutine levels
  1648 total uops in 8087 microcode ROM
  looks like "add to exponent" — is not
